{"id": "unknown-2026-09-24-011", "date": "2026-09-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Second-life PV modules turned into solar balconies in Germany", "content": "<p>A reuse project in Kassel, Germany, has repurposed 300 used solar modules to create 150 balcony PV systems, with tiered pricing aimed at improving affordability. The 13-year-old panels were inspected and refurbished, with local organizations providing technical, logistical and financial support.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/24/second-life-pv-modules-turned-into-solar-balconies-in-germany/\">Second-life PV modules turned into solar balconies in Germany</a> appear", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/24/second-life-pv-modules-turned-into-solar-balconies-in-germany/", "type": "rss"}]}
